# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Data & trained models
#
# None of this belongs in git: it totals ~378 MB, and
# data/raw/ais_2023H2.parquet alone is 154 MB, which exceeds GitHub's
# 100 MB per-file hard limit (the push would be rejected outright).
# Large blobs also stay in history forever once committed.
#
# All of it is reproducible from the scripts in pipeline/:
#   clean_datasets.py            -> data/cleaned/
#   build_*_features.py          -> data/features/
#   merge_congestion_datasets.py -> data/features/
#   train_*.py, pipeline.py      -> models/saved_models/, data/processed/
# Source datasets go in data/raw/ (see README for where each came from).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
data/raw/*
# ...except the tiny ingestion fallback that MaritimeClient loads by
# default. Without it a fresh clone has no offline event source.
!data/raw/example.json

# Derived files are not tracked (rebuild them with the pipeline/ scripts) EXCEPT the
# few the running app reads, so a fresh clone works without the raw datasets.
data/cleaned/*
!data/cleaned/port_congestion.csv
data/features/*
!data/features/transit_journeys.csv
!data/features/transit_journeys_summary.json
data/processed/
models/saved_models/*.joblib
!models/saved_models/risk_model.joblib
!models/saved_models/congestion_model.joblib
!models/saved_models/fuel_model.joblib
!models/saved_models/anomaly_model.joblib
# The metrics each train_*.py script saves next to its model ARE tracked:
# the Evaluation page reads them.
pipeline/.cache/
